# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest, and reproduces production's snapshot-load
# failure path. TryRehydrateFromSnapshotAsync answers an ordinary storage fault,
# a missing segment or an unreadable frame by returning false, which the
# activation cannot tell from "no snapshot": it takes the -1 cold override and
# replays the whole READABLE WAL. Under coverage-gated trim the readable WAL no
# longer holds the prefix the snapshot covered, and the cold-replay guard only
# fires when the tail has passed the persisted checkpoint plus one, so a tail
# sitting at exactly that boundary passes. The leaf comes up having read past
# acknowledged writes it does not hold. The base fails the activation instead.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestLoadFailureColdReplays
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a snapshot that fails to load is treated as absent and the leaf cold-replays a WAL trimmed under that snapshot's coverage
PERTURBS: ActivateLoadFail

--- FIND
    /\ snapCov[l] # NoSnap
    /\ faults < MaxFaults
    /\ faults' = faults + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED leafVars
    /\ UNCHANGED pinVars
--- REPLACE
    /\ snapCov[l] # NoSnap
    /\ faults < MaxFaults
    /\ faults' = faults + 1
\* MUTATION: the failed load falls through to the cold path, guarded only by
\* production's cold-replay trim test against the durable checkpoint.
    /\ ~FallsOff(durCp[l])
    /\ up' = [up EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
    /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![l] = {}]
    /\ rp' = [rp EXCEPT ![l] = -1]
    /\ stCp' = [stCp EXCEPT ![l] = durCp[l]]
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durCp, clk, cov, snapCov, snapRows, stale>>
    /\ UNCHANGED pinVars
--- END
